Falsifies `program_argument_contract::verification::a_parsed_page_holds_exactly_what_its_header_states`.

The defect: the record walk reads to the end of the page instead of to the `total` the header
states, so bytes after the records count as records whenever they happen to parse.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(sum, total)`, on a page whose trailing bytes form
whole records beyond `total`.

diff --git a/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/program_argument_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@
         if total > room {
             return None;
         }
-        let records = &page[HEADER_BYTES..HEADER_BYTES + total];
+        let records = &page[HEADER_BYTES..];
         // Walk every record now, so the iterator below can never meet a length that overruns. The
         // walk runs until the records are used up, so its bound is the slice (each record takes at
         // least four bytes) and not a count the page chose, and the number walked must then equal
